# oracle: RHEO 2d ice cube pour, cut down from examples/rheo/ice-cubes (the same 50 x 100 box with 588 fluid atoms instead of 1470, 4 deposited 100-atom cubes instead of 8, 1200 steps instead of 30000, thermo every 200): atom_style hybrid rheo/thermal bond, fix rheo thermal shift surface/detection, fix rheo/thermal with conductivity, specific/heat, Tfreeze, latent/heat and react (bond creation on freezing and breaking on melting), pair hybrid/overlay rheo and rheo/solid, bond bpm/spring, create_bonds many, fix deposit mol, wall/region and gravity
# oracle-inputs: w96rheo_icecubes_square.mol
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=2e-6 abs=1e-12 atomrel=1e-8
# Measured with native LAMMPS, engine vs native over the 1200 steps: the surface normals, the layer and surface status, the shift velocities, the density and the forces now follow native's newton-off half-list order (compute_rheo_surface, compute_rheo_grad and compute_rheo_vshift sum the pairs in native's order, and the layer test follows native's partner rule), so positions, velocities, forces, densities and every thermo ke row agree to the rounding level: max thermo ke 2.0e-15 relative, per-atom scaled errors (max(1,|value|)) xu 1.0e-14, yu 1.9e-14, vx 2.4e-14, vy 1.9e-14, fx 7.4e-14, fy 1.7e-14. The one open difference is the press of the last row (step 1200): 1.2e-6 relative, which is an absolute 6e-11 in the virial (pxx and pyy +6e-11, pxy -6e-11, from one term not yet traced; press at rows 200 to 1100 agrees to 1e-15). The tolerance is therefore 2e-6 relative on thermo (abs 1e-12) and 1e-8 on the atoms.
units        lj
dimension    2
atom_style   hybrid rheo/thermal bond
boundary     m m p
comm_modify  vel yes
newton       off
special_bonds lj 0.0 1.0 1.0 coul 1.0 1.0 1.0

region       box block -25 25 0 100 -0.01 0.01 units box
create_box   1 box bond/types 1 extra/bond/per/atom 15 extra/special/per/atom 50

region       fluid block -24 24 1 12 EDGE EDGE units box
lattice      sq 1.0
create_atoms 1 region fluid

set          group all sph/e 8.0

variable     cut equal 3.0
variable     n equal 1.0
variable     rho0 equal 1.0
variable     cs equal 1.0
variable     mp equal ${rho0}/${n}
variable     zeta equal 0.05
variable     kappa equal 0.01*${rho0}/${mp}
variable     eta equal 0.05
variable     Cv equal 1.0
variable     L equal 1.0
variable     Tf equal 1.0

mass         * ${mp}
timestep     0.1

pair_style   hybrid/overlay rheo ${cut} artificial/visc ${zeta} rheo/solid
pair_coeff   * * rheo
pair_coeff   * * rheo/solid 1.0 1.0 1.0

bond_style   bpm/spring
bond_coeff   1 1.0 1.0 1.0

molecule     my_mol "w96rheo_icecubes_square.mol"

region       wall block EDGE EDGE EDGE EDGE -5 5 side in open 4 units box
region       drop block -16 16 70 90 EDGE EDGE side in units box

fix          1 all rheo ${cut} quintic 0 thermal shift surface/detection coordination 22 8
fix          2 all rheo/viscosity * constant ${eta}
fix          3 all rheo/pressure * linear
fix          4 all rheo/thermal conductivity * constant ${kappa} specific/heat * constant ${Cv} Tfreeze * constant ${Tf} latent/heat * constant ${L} react 1.5 1
fix          5 all wall/region wall harmonic 1.0 1.0 1.0
fix          6 all gravity 2e-4 vector 0 -1 0
fix          7 all deposit 4 0 300 37241459 mol my_mol region drop near 2.0 vy -0.02 -0.02
fix          8 all enforce2d

compute      rho all rheo/property/atom rho
compute      phase all rheo/property/atom phase
compute      temp all rheo/property/atom temperature
compute      eng all rheo/property/atom energy
compute      nbond all nbond/atom

thermo       200
thermo_style custom step time ke press atoms
thermo_modify format float %.15g
run          1200
